ock\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Learn how to get started</a>.\"},{\"kind\":\"review_comment\",\"author\":\"copilot-pull-request-reviewer\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-06-01T15:12:48.000Z\",\"state\":null,\"path\":\"packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/test-results/filter/filter-context.tsx\",\"line\":146,\"body\":\"The new de-duplication behavior (keying by conceptUuid instead of flatName) isn’t covered by the existing filter-context unit tests. Without a targeted test case, regressions (e.g., reintroducing flatName-based keys) could slip in unnoticed.\\n\\nConsider adding a test where two different tree leaves have different flatName values but the same conceptUuid and identical obs (same obsDatetime + value), and assert that tableData contains only one entry for that observation.\"},{\"kind\":\"review\",\"author\":\"denniskigen\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-06-02T20:24:09.000Z\",\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"path\":null,\"line\":null,\"body\":\"\"},{\"kind\":\"review_comment\",\"author\":\"denniskigen\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-06-02T20:24:10.000Z\",\"state\":null,\"path\":\"packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/test-results/filter/filter-context.tsx\",\"line\":145,\"body\":\"Thanks for tackling this. On dev3, `/obstree` can return the same observation through multiple branches, so deduping is the right direction. I think this key is a bit too broad because it dedupes before we group rows by the rendered panel. The current CI failure shows this with the existing `mockResults` fixture: the Complete blood count panel, Platelets included, is mounted under two top-level roots, Hematology and Bloodwork, so the same observations appear under both. Keying only on concept identity keeps the first and drops the second, which reduces the tree view from 3 tables to 2 and the Platelets rows from 2 to 1. \\r\\n\\r\\nCould we scope the dedupe to the rendered group as well, for example include the group key derived from `flatName`, or dedupe after grouping? A focused regression test for this fixture shape would also help lock the intended behavior in.\"},{\"kind\":\"issue_comment\",\"author\":\"NethmiRodrigo\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-06-10T05:02:02.000Z\",\"state\":null,\"path\":null,\"line\":null,\"body\":\"@denniskigen could you re-review this? I missed this before and I think it would be good if we can get this in, if it looks good\"},{\"kind\":\"review\",\"author\":\"jayasanka-sack\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-06-10T06:24:13.000Z\",\"state\":\"APPROVED\",\"path\":null,\"line\":null,\"body\":\"Looks good to me, thanks @cerveaubleu64 and @NethmiRodrigo!\"}],\"freshness\":[{\"repo\":\"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart\",\"lastSyncedAt\":\"2026-10-24T04:03:34.106Z\",\"stale\":false}],\"nextOffset\":null,\"truncated\":[]}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015PdJBcS3S6vWiM8xZvMK1G","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
