{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgLQZA9u7C2ikoEJYqPJH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The de-duplication was reworked in PR #3374, a follow-up to #3345. The root cause is that `/obstree` returns the same observation under several branches (Bloodwork contains Hematology, and each root carries a full copy of the obs list). Keying on `flatName` and concatenating copies showed one Platelets result as two. The fix treats whole obs lists as the unit of de-duplication:\n\n- **`filter-reducer.ts`** merges same-`flatName` duplicates with a multiset union, keeping the highest count of each `obsDatetime|value` seen in any single branch, instead of concatenating. It also copies nodes rather than mutating the SWR-cached trees. (`mergeObsMultisetMax` at lines 11–39.)\n- **`filter-context.tsx`** builds a normalized branch list keyed by rendered panel plus `conceptUuid` (via `deriveGroupKey`). Duplicate branches are collapsed with the same merge. `tableData`, `timelineData`, and both result counts all derive from this list, so the header count matches the rows. (Lines 39–47 and 113–132.)\n- **`tree-view` and `grouped-timeline`** match checkbox filters against all contributing `flatNames`, so filtering by either alias of a collapsed branch keeps its row visible.\n\nTwo things it does not solve: `obsDatetime + value` still cannot tell a copy from two real results with the same value and time, and that limitation is documented in the code. The fix for that is server-side. The PR's \"Other\" section proposes adding obs `uuid` to the obstree response (`ObsTreeResource1_9` in the REST module), which would make de-duplication exact. That became ticket **RESTWS-1038**, per a comment from denniskigen. REST PR #751, \"RESTWS-1038: Include obs uuid in the obstree response\", is open and references it. I did not confirm the ticket in Jira itself.\n\nThe change that answers the question is PR #3374 (merge commit `d47d346`). The earlier PR #3345 (merge commit `16600fb`) switched the key from `flatName` to `conceptUuid`, which was the first step and is what #3374 corrects for the Hematology/Bloodwork overlap.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"repo\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart\", \"pr\": 3374},\n  {\"repo\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart\", \"commit\": \"d47d346cc105c4c72dfb1ce68a05abbcb1ad4f84\"},\n  {\"ticket\": \"RESTWS-1038\"},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/test-results/filter/filter-reducer.ts\", \"startLine\": 11, \"endLine\": 39},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/test-results/filter/filter-context.tsx\", \"startLine\": 113, \"endLine\": 132},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-tests-app/src/test-results/filter/filter-context.tsx\", \"startLine\": 39, \"endLine\": 47},\n  {\"repo\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart\", \"pr\": 3345},\n  {\"repo\": \"openmrs-ębmodule-webservices.rest\", \"pr\": 751},\n  {\"repo\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart\", \"commit\": \"16600fbfd85e41b98eaaa84817293a6b9e2af65f\"}\n]\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6689,"cache_read_input_tokens":26410,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6689},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"db92f199-38ea-4dc1-ac25-e531b6f4601b","uuid":"c0542d66-64e4-4370-a31e-2275edbd70bc","timestamp":"2026-10-24T04:10:11.298Z","request_id":"req_011CgLQZ9sHYHeYZsbfG5Koh"}
